docs {
  Staff-only flows for authoring an event's visual theme ("diseño de la
  experiencia") — T3/T3b/T4, `odd/tasks/theme-authoring.md`. A future
  interview skill reads these `.bru` files to learn which endpoints to call,
  in what order, and what payload shapes to send.

  ## Layer model

  A resolved theme is always the merge of, in order:

    SystemDefault (code, `src/events/theme/system-default.theme.ts`)
      -> Brillipoint default (code, `src/events/theme/brillipoint-default.ts`)
      -> preset (`event_themes`, picked via `eventThemeId`)
      -> event overrides (`events.theme_overrides`)

  SystemDefault is ALWAYS the base — an event with no preset still renders
  a complete theme. Removing a preset assignment never breaks resolution;
  it just falls back further up the chain.

  ## Flows

  - `party/`: a couple/individual picks a preset and layers per-event
    overrides on top (cover image, confetti). `socialCta` falls back to the
    Brillipoint default automatically.
  - Company events are authored per event the same way: store the company
    name in `honoreesNames` and set colors, images, `socialCta` and
    `rewardPromo` in the event's `themeOverrides`. No preset is required.

  ## Rules that apply to every step below

  - `PATCH` on overrides/tokens/images (preset `tokens`/`images`, event
    `themeOverrides`) REPLACES the stored value
    entirely — it is never deep-merged with what was there before. Omit a
    field to leave it untouched; send it to replace it whole.
  - Image flow: create the owner first (preset / reference an existing
    event) -> `POST /theme-assets/upload-url` -> `PUT` the file to
    the returned `signedUrl` -> store `{ path, url: publicUrl }` in the
    matching `images.<slot>`. We host every theme image ourselves; a client-
    supplied external URL is never stored.
  - `image/svg+xml` is only accepted for the `logo`, `splashIcon` and
    `watermark` slots (422 otherwise); `image/png`/`jpeg`/`webp` are
    accepted everywhere.
  - The `cover` slot must be 4:5 — validated by the frontend before upload,
    not by this API.
  - `POST /events/themes/preview` is a dry run: `{ eventTheme, warnings }`.
    Nothing is persisted. `warnings` carries non-blocking contrast issues
    computed on the RESOLVED tokens (e.g. overrides that set `primary`
    against an inherited `onPrimary`) — review them before saving, but they never
    block the preview itself.
  - `socialCta` falls back to the Brillipoint default whenever the event
    supplies no usable block — an event without an event-level `socialCta`
    override still gets a usable CTA.
  - The public theme endpoint (`GET /events/{token}/theme`) is cached for
    5 minutes — changes made in this flow may take up to 5 minutes to show
    there even though `preview`/staff reads see them immediately.

  ## Preset assignment

  `PATCH /events/:id` accepts `eventThemeId` (preset id, 404
  `EVENT_THEME_NOT_FOUND` if unknown) or `null` to remove the preset and
  render on the SystemDefault base layer. `party/05` assigns the preset
  picked in `party/01`.
}
